course: dictionary
lesson: 11834
title: Blameless: not at fault
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Blameless means not to blame. If something bad happened and it was not your fault, you are blameless. It can also mean you have never done anything wrong, so you are innocent and good.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Sam had not touched the vase, so he was blameless when it broke.» Sam did not do it, so nobody can blame him. Ask yourself: would «not at fault» fit in the same place? If it does, you have found the meaning.
explain: Blameless is often used when someone's name is cleared. «The judge found the farmer completely blameless.» You can also talk about a whole life: to lead a blameless life means to live with no wrongdoing.
fact: Blameless means not responsible for something bad, or never doing anything wrong.
fact: The ending -less means without, so blameless means without blame.
fact: «She was blameless» means she was not at fault.
fact: Blameless is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a person, a life or a record.
fact: Innocent is a close synonym for the second meaning, but blameless is often used about accidents and arguments.
exercise: «Sam had not touched the vase, so he was blameless when it broke.» What does blameless mean here? | Late for school | *Not at fault | Very angry | Covered in paint
exercise: «The baker led a blameless life and never told a lie.» Which word is closest in meaning to blameless? | Careless | *Innocent | Hungry | Loud
exercise: In «The old dog was blameless», which word does blameless describe? | was | *dog | old | the
test: «Nobody could blame Mia, so she was blameless.» What does blameless mean? | Tired | *Not to blame | Clumsy | Excited
test: Which phrase means living with no wrongdoing? | Lead a late life | *Lead a blameless life | Lead a noisy life | Lead a hungry life
exam: Choose the meaning of blameless in «The court found him blameless.» | Ready | *Not guilty | Guilty | Lost
